      "raw": "<p>Yesterday I ran into a fight against advanced Plague Rat which went absolutely completely out-of-control. I was playing with the complete F5 and it resulted in Plague Rat doing 85 damage to the heroes in just one turn!</p><p>Advanced Plage Rat (+1 damage) had Plague Locus (+1 damage) and Shadowy Ambush (Play a villain card when PR does +5 damage) in play. The fight was in the Realm of Discord with Imbued Frailty (+1 damage) in play. Because of +3 damage dealt by PG and H=5, every one-shot of PR resulted in an extra villain card play. So in PG&#39;s third turn, he played consecutively:</p><p>Vicious Onslaught -&gt; Ravage -&gt; Noxious Bite -&gt; Vicious Onslaught -&gt; Tooth &amp; Claw -&gt; Tooth &amp; Claw -&gt; Noxious Bite. Also, all infections cards, 2 Afflicted Frenzy cards and 1 Bestial Vitality.</p><p>Even with Legacy having played Heroic Interception his previous turn (!), at the end of PG&#39;s turn the result was:</p><p>Legacy: 21 -&gt; 0 HP<br />Tachyon: 15 -&gt; 0 HP<br />Bunker: 17 -&gt; 6 HP<br />Wraith: 20 -&gt; 2 HP<br />AZ: 23 -&gt; 4 HP</p><p>With all the heroes infected and multiple ongoings of PG on the table, it&#39;s not necessary to mention the outcome of this battle.. I could only smile when I saw PG dominating me.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This led me thinking whether it is possible to play all of PG&#39;s cards in just 2 turns. Turns out, even without the aid of the environment and without any major DR to the heroes: yes, advanced PR is able to do that (even with H=3). For this, his turns has to be like this:</p><p>Turn 1:&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Shadowy Ambush<br />Turn 2: Tooth &amp; Claw -&gt; Shadowy Ambush. After that, PG plays 2 cards every time he deals +5 damage, and still has to do the second damage by Tooth &amp; Claw (resulting in 2 card play). If always at least one of these 2 cards is a Tooth &amp; Claw or Noxious Bite, it will be a train unstopapble. I calculated that for H=5, this will be 199 damage done by PR in just 2 turns.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Of course this is a very specific set-up, but it is crazy to realise a villain can play his complete deck in just 2 turns. Also, you can imagine that even with a less optimal set-up, a situation like this can be devastating, like my experience yesterday. &nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">So, it rests me to say: all hail the Plague Rat!</span></p>",
